---

<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Samla site — framework consumption check</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/samla.css" />
    <script src="/assets/js/samla.js" defer></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="container" style="padding-block: var(--space-8)">
      <h1 class="text-page-title">Proving /site consumes the real Samla framework</h1>
      <p class="text-lead">No copied CSS or JS lives in this project — everything below is the actual samla.css and samla.js served from the repo root via a symlink.</p>

      <section class="stack" data-gap="5" style="margin-top: var(--space-7)">
        <div class="cluster" data-gap="4">
          <button class="button" type="button">Primary button</button>
          <button class="button" type="button" data-variant="secondary">Secondary button</button>
          <a class="link" href="#accordion">A real link</a>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion" id="accordion">
          <details class="accordion__item" name="check" open>
            <summary class="accordion__trigger">Is this the real accordion primitive?<span class="accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="accordion__panel"><p>Yes — this is assets/css/primitives/accordion.css and samla.js's initAccordion, loaded from the framework root, not duplicated into /site.</p></div>
          </details>
          <details class="accordion__item" name="check">
            <summary class="accordion__trigger">Where do the styles come from?<span class="accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
            <div class="accordion__panel"><p><code>/assets/css/samla.css</code>, symlinked from <code>site/public/assets</code> to the repo root's <code>assets/</code>.</p></div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" data-surface="alternate" style="margin-top: var(--space-8)">
        <div class="container">
          <header class="section-header" data-align="stack">
            <h2 class="section-header__title text-section-heading">A real Hero, for good measure</h2>
          </header>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
